From cf867226d3658d682eaade99e5e090a90a08b26e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Juan Manuel Lopez Carrillo <juanmanuellopezcarrillo@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 13:50:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 061/130] drm/sun4i: sun55i_de: DE reset pulse in mode_set
 (fix MBUS wedge)

An MBUS port fault of the DE during a session teardown (fb freed with fetch
in flight) leaves an unacked transaction that hangs the port: the registers
read correct but the fetch is dead (only the background color shows) and in
the worst case it drags the interconnect. SDDM triggered it on every start.
reset_control_reset of the DE core on entering mode_set aborts the stuck
transaction; all state is rewritten right after (top MMIO + full RCQ reload).
Replaces the manual pulse of the de-bringup.service (C4C) at the right point
in the driver.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun55i_de.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun55i_de.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun55i_de.c
index e053a1d5e..6b8495b1f 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun55i_de.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun55i_de.c
@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@
 #include <linux/math64.h>
 #include <linux/moduleparam.h>
 #include <linux/of_reserved_mem.h>
+#include <linux/reset.h>
 #include <linux/preempt.h>	/* in_hardirq() — TEMP instrumentation */
 #include <linux/spinlock.h>
 
@@ -565,6 +566,19 @@ void sun55i_de_mode_set(struct sun8i_mixer *mixer,
 	u32 w = mode->hdisplay, h = mode->vdisplay;
 	u32 size = SUN55I_DE_OUT_SIZE(w, h);
 	u32 vtotal = mode->crtc_vtotal, clock = mode->crtc_clock;
+
+	/*
+	 * DE core reset pulse (bit in DE_RESET 0x8000, the mixer reset via
+	 * display_clocks) BEFORE reprogramming: if an MBUS port transaction
+	 * got stuck from a fault in the previous teardown (session change,
+	 * SDDM), only the reset aborts it; without this the DE stays wedged
+	 * (correct registers, dead fetch -> fixed background) until a reboot.
+	 * Equivalent to the manual pulse of the de-bringup.service from C4C,
+	 * done at the right place: every CRTC (re)enable. Safe here: all
+	 * state is rewritten right after (top via MMIO + full RCQ reload of
+	 * the full_arms).
+	 */
+	reset_control_reset(mixer->reset);
 	u32 vbp;
 	u32 mux;
 
